# The fixes to step 28, from its independent review: variation selectors
# kept out of the system prompt.

[break] one-line-keeps-selectors
rule: `one_line` keeps no variation selector, neither a run after a character, which can carry any bytes unseen into section 6 (a skill's name and description, a source's description), nor one after each character, a byte each.
file: crates/cineris-base/src/visible.rs
in: one_line
find: !acts_unseen(character) && !is_selector(character)
replace: !acts_unseen(character)
packages: cineris-base, cineris-ext
caught-by:
    cineris-base visible::tests::one_line_keeps_no_variation_selector
    cineris-ext skills::tests::no_variation_selector_of_a_skill_reaches_the_index

[break] plain-keeps-selectors
rule: Section 6's skills part and every section 7 text keep no variation selector.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/context/prompt.rs
in: plain
find: acts_unseen(unseen) || is_selector(unseen)
replace: acts_unseen(unseen)
packages: cineris-agent
caught-by:
    cineris-agent context::prompt::tests::no_variation_selector_reaches_the_index_or_a_text
    cineris-agent::it extensions::no_variation_selector_reaches_the_prompt

[break] a-skills-path-keeps-its-selector
rule: A skill's path is written for the model with every variation selector as an escape, so that the system prompt, which keeps none, still names the file.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
find: visible_to_the_model(&name.to_string_lossy())
replace: visible(&name.to_string_lossy())
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_skills_path_holds_its_selector_as_an_escape

# From mutations/step-28-fixes-guards.breaks (part `guards`).
# The fixes to step 28's guards of the harness's own approvals, from its
# independent review (findings 1, 2, 3, 7, 17 and 19): `cineris project`'s
# changes, `auth login` and `logout` and `stats reset` refused under a
# session's command; the Windows walks that fell open at their bound; the
# RPC socket refusing any harness's commands; a harness that is process 1;
# `ProgramData` among the variables that move the stores; and each of
# those variables shown refused.
#
# The breaks of code only Windows builds carry `os: windows`; run them on a
# runner: gh workflow run try --ref <branch> -f os=windows -f command="mutate <break>"

[break] project-change-not-under-a-session
rule: `cineris project accept`, `disable`, `delete` and `promote` refuse under a session's command before anything is read.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
find: crate::not_under_a_session(name, &format!("project {action}"))?;
replace: let _ = action;
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system nested::sys_cineris_run_by_a_sessions_command_is_held_or_refused

[break] project-add-not-under-a-session
rule: `cineris project add` refuses under a session's command before anything is read.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
find: crate::not_under_a_session(name, "project add")?
replace: {}
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system nested::sys_cineris_run_by_a_sessions_command_is_held_or_refused

[break] auth-login-not-under-a-session
rule: `cineris auth login` refuses under a session's command before anything is read.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
find: crate::not_under_a_session(name, "auth login")?
replace: {}
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system nested::sys_cineris_run_by_a_sessions_command_is_held_or_refused

[break] stats-reset-not-under-a-session
rule: `cineris stats reset` refuses under a session's command before anything is read.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/commands.rs
find: crate::not_under_a_session(name, "stats reset")?;
replace: let _ = name;
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system nested::sys_cineris_run_by_a_sessions_command_is_held_or_refused

[break] service-walk-falls-open-at-its-bound
rule: On Windows a service's start through more command interpreters and runtimes than the walk reads is not known, which refuses, and not "no service".
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
find: Under::Unknown(past)
replace: { let _ = past; Under::Nothing }
packages: cineris-sandbox
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::tests::a_services_start_through_more_interpreters_than_the_bound_is_not_known

[break] line-of-parents-falls-open-at-its-bound
rule: On Windows a line of parents that goes on past the 64 processes it reads is not known, which refuses where nothing holds the process.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
find: Runs::Unknown(past)
replace: { let _ = past; Runs::No }
packages: cineris-sandbox
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::tests::the_line_of_parents_is_read_through_any_program_to_its_end

[break] walk-stops-before-process-1
rule: On Linux the line of parents ends only at process 0 or at a process that is its own parent: a harness that is process 1 is seen.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
in: walk
find: if at == 0 {
replace: if at <= 1 {
