os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::tests::a_harness_that_is_process_1_is_seen_and_the_line_ends_at_process_0

[break] stores-harness-stops-before-process-1
rule: On Linux the session's process whose environment a nested run's stores are compared with is found when it is process 1.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
in: harnesses_on_the_line
find: if at == 0 {
replace: if at <= 1 {
packages: cineris-sandbox, cineris-cli
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::tests::the_harnesses_of_a_line_are_every_one_to_process_0

[break] stores-not-compared-without-a-harness
rule: On Linux, under a session's command whose harness is not found on the line, a nested run's stores cannot be compared with the session's, and it is refused.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
find: return Some("the session's own environment, whose process was not found,".to_owned());
replace: return None;
packages: cineris-cli
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system guards::sys_a_nested_run_whose_line_cannot_be_read_is_refused_with_its_stores_moved

[break] a-peers-line-is-not-read
rule: On Linux another process's line of parents is read as this process's own, from its parent up.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
find: Seen::Of { parent, .. } => walk(parent, |pid| seen(&own, pid), false),
replace: Seen::Of { .. } => Under::Nothing,
packages: cineris-sandbox
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::sys::tests::sys_another_processs_line_is_read_as_this_ones

[break] serve-passes-no-peer-check
rule: `cineris serve` refuses at the socket a client under any harness's session's command, read as the approving subcommands read their own process.
